target:    wp-slimstat.php
gate:      php tests/purge-archive-order-test.php
kind:      name-only
expect:    still assigns PurgeArchive::STATS_COLUMNS / EVENT_COLUMNS
rationale: The intersection is still computed - copyableColumns() is called, the plan is built, the lost/usable checks below still run - and then the result is thrown away and the manifest constants are used to build the SQL anyway. That is the shipped defect with the fix sitting one line above it, and a gate that only asked whether copyableColumns appeared would pass. The archive tables are declared reconcile => false, so on an upgraded install the manifest names ua_id and the archive has never had it; the probe errors, probeForCollision() reads that as cannot-tell, and retention stops on every tick forever while blaming utf8mb4.
---
--- a/wp-slimstat.php
+++ b/wp-slimstat.php
@@ -1853,8 +1853,8 @@
             $event_plan = \SlimStat\Utils\PurgeArchive::copyableColumns($db, $prefix, 'slim_events');
             $stats_plan = \SlimStat\Utils\PurgeArchive::copyableColumns($db, $prefix, 'slim_stats');
 
-            $event_columns = $event_plan['copy'];
-            $stats_columns = $stats_plan['copy'];
+            $event_columns = \SlimStat\Utils\PurgeArchive::EVENT_COLUMNS;
+            $stats_columns = \SlimStat\Utils\PurgeArchive::STATS_COLUMNS;
 
             if ($event_plan['lost'] || $stats_plan['lost']) {
                 self::record_degradation('purge (archive schema)',
